# Queue Pi (RabbitMQ)

This service hosts the RabbitMQ broker used by all sensor Pis and the central Pi.

## Quick start

1) Start RabbitMQ:

docker compose up -d

2) Open the management UI:

http://<queue-pi-ip>:15672

## Defaults

- Admin user: admin / adminpass
- Sensor user: sensor / sensorpass
- Vhost: sensors_vhost
- AMQP port: 5672
- Management UI: 15672
- Prometheus: 9090
- Grafana: 3000
- Queue monitor API: 9000
- Node exporter: 9100
- RabbitMQ metrics: 15692
  (used by Prometheus and Grafana)

## Connection string examples

- Central Pi consumer:
  amqp://sensor:sensorpass@<queue-pi-ip>:5672/sensors_vhost

## Notes

- Change default credentials before deploying to production.
- The RabbitMQ definitions are loaded from:
  ./rabbitmq/definitions.json
- If you change RabbitMQ credentials, update `queue_pi/docker-compose.yml`
  for the queue-monitor and Grafana admin user/password.
- Prometheus scrapes RabbitMQ metrics from:
  http://<queue-pi-ip>:15692/metrics
- Queue monitor exposes:
  http://<queue-pi-ip>:9000/health
  http://<queue-pi-ip>:9000/metrics
- Grafana auto-provisions a Prometheus data source and a
  "Queue Pi Overview" dashboard.

## Install script

Run from the repo root:

sudo bash queue_pi/scripts/install.sh